+---
+id: task-003-validate-task-input
+type: task
+title: "Validate task input"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Validate task input
+
+Some screens pass what the user typed straight to the list, so odd tasks can appear. The list must
+reject invalid input with a clear error that says what is wrong.
+
+## What it asks
+
+- A title that is empty, or only spaces, is rejected.
+- A title longer than 120 characters is rejected.
+- A priority other than `low`, `normal` or `high` is rejected.
+- A tag that is empty, or contains a space, is rejected.
+- This applies when a task is added, renamed or tagged.
+- When input is rejected, nothing in the list changes.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- **Rejected input returns a `Result` error** (`r4-errors-as-result`), with a new error code,
+  `invalid-input`, and a message that says what is wrong, for example `the title is longer than 120
+  characters`.
+- **The title is checked after trimming**, the same way it is stored: `"  Buy milk "` is accepted as
+  `"Buy milk"`, and `"   "` is rejected as empty. The 120 characters are counted on the trimmed title.
+- **A tag may not contain any whitespace character**, not only the space: a tab or a line break makes a
+  tag as broken as a space does. Tags are not trimmed, so `" garden"` is rejected rather than changed.
+- **Untagging is not checked**: it removes a tag and cannot add an invalid one.
+- **Validation runs before the lookup**, so a rename to an invalid title on an unknown task reports the
+  invalid title.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- `add` rejects a blank title, a title over 120 characters, an unknown priority, and a blank or
+  space-containing tag, each with `invalid-input` and a message naming the problem.
+- `add` accepts a title of exactly 120 characters.
+- `rename` and `tag` reject the same invalid input, and the task keeps its title, tags and `updatedAt`.
+- A rejected `add` adds no task, and `list` and `openCount` stay as they were.
+- Valid input keeps working as before.
